    "vernacular": "Dense city of low and mid-rise reinforced-concrete and concrete-block buildings, often unfinished with rebar on the roof, painted in bright blues, yellows, pinks and greens, with flat roofs and corrugated metal on informal hillside housing; older neighbourhoods keep Haitian gingerbread houses (timber, deep porches, fretwork, steep roofs, tall shutters). Public buildings are French-influenced white neoclassical or Beaux-Arts. Post-2010 rebuilding is plain and functional. Palms, mango and almond trees, open plazas, hot hazy light.",
